    <string name="asynctask_explanation">📌 Why was AsyncTask deprecated in Android 11?\n\n• Memory leaks: AsyncTask holds an implicit reference to the Activity.\n• Ignored lifecycle: keeps running even if the Activity is destroyed.\n• Serial execution by default since Android 3.0 (one task after another).\n• Results delivered to dead activities → NullPointerException.\n\n✅ Alternatives: ExecutorService + Handler, WorkManager, or Coroutines.</string>
    
